# Execution guardrail

- Verify work with `scripts/check.sh`. One run is one cycle. You get at most two failed runs per branch.
- Between runs, make one focused fix. Never weaken, skip, or delete tests, and never loosen lint or type settings, to get a pass.
- Never reset or delete the guardrail state, which lives under the agent state folder at the repo root. A hook blocks it, and only Victor resets it.
- When the script prints `GUARDRAIL` or a hook blocks a check, stop working on the code and write a failure report:

```markdown
# ISSUE-<n> FAILED

- Ticket: #<n> <title>
- Branch: <branch>
- Goal: <one sentence>
- What I tried: <one bullet per attempt>
- Failing command: <command>
- Error output: <last ~60 lines, fenced>
- Likely cause: <best guess>
- Files touched: <paths>
- Suggested next step: <what a human should look at first>
```

- Local agent: save it as `.agent-reports/ISSUE-<n>-FAILED.md`. It is gitignored.
- Cloud agent: push the work, open the pull request as a draft, post the report as a pull request comment, and add the `needs-human` label to the issue.
- Then stop and wait. Do not start another fix.
